## 4. GROUND TRUTH API — DO NOT INVENT

Source of truth is `scriptbysumothemofo.lua`. These are the ONLY methods you may use unless user asks for a custom extension (then build it in same style):

```lua
ImGui.new(toggleKey: Enum.KeyCode?) --> gui object (.Gui: ScreenGui)
gui:Window(title: string, pos: Vector2, width: number?) --> W
W:Tab(name: string) --> Container

Container:Text(str)
Container:Separator()
Container:Button(label, callback)
Container:Checkbox(label, default, callback) --> { Get() }
Container:SliderFloat(label, min, max, default, callback) --> { Get() }
Container:CollapsingHeader(label, open: boolean?) --> Container (nested body)
```

Key facts:
- ScreenGui: Name="ImGuiLib", ResetOnSpawn=false, DisplayOrder=100, parent = LocalPlayer PlayerGui. Toggle = RightShift default.
- Draggable title bar (mouse + touch). Auto-sizing Y. Don't hardcode window height.
- Tabs auto-select first tab. Tab width = `#name * 9 + 16`.
- Theme: bg 15,15,18 / title 41,74,122 / frame 32,48,74 / accent 66,150,250 / btn 45,90,150 / text 235,235,235 / border 60,60,75. Font Code.
- Event-driven, no RenderStep. Slider uses math.clamp + UIS drag. Checkbox row = TextButton for big hitbox.

Starter template you should reuse:
```lua
-- IMGUI port made by @sumothemofo (https://github.com/justatiretbh/Roblox-IMGUI)
print("IMGUI port made by @sumothemofo")

local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local ImGuiModule = require(ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("ImGui"))

local gui = ImGuiModule.new(Enum.KeyCode.RightShift)
local w = gui:Window("Dear Roblox GUI", Vector2.new(40, 60), 300)

local main = w:Tab("Main")
main:Text("DearIMGUI")
main:Separator()
main:Checkbox("Show crosshair", true, function(on) print("crosshair", on) end)
main:SliderFloat("FOV", 50, 120, 70, function(v) workspace.CurrentCamera.FieldOfView = v end)
main:Button("Reset", function() print("reset") end)

local misc = w:Tab("Misc")
local h = misc:CollapsingHeader("Audio", true)
h:SliderFloat("Volume", 0, 1, 0.5, function(v) print("vol", v) end)
```

